{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789213421,"nonce":"oAtB15+i5nVd1VeC7ZTcmp3B9nE=","title":"Port ash's Immix heap into caribou as the core heap","message":"std/src/gc.rs (about 6k lines) becomes caribou::heap, behaviour-preserving.\nIts coupling to the rest of ash_std is small: hl layouts (now caribou_abi),\nper-thread exception cells (ExcState, with_exc, gc_swap_exc_state) that belong\nto the adapter and are not roots, a call to fiber::request_fiber_poll (becomes\na registered hook), hlp_type_size (pure, moves to caribou_abi), one nightly\nAPI (OnceLock::get_mut_or_init) that stable code replaces, and the\ncurrent_exception / exception_handler fields on ImmixAllocator, which leave\nthe heap.\n\nKeep the hlp_gc_* and hl_register_thread C exports in ash_std as thin\nforwarders during the transition so HDLLs and the interpreter see no change.\n\nAdditions once the port is green: allocation kinds honoured (Raw scanned\nconservatively, NoPtr never scanned, Typed with an optional trace hook read\nfrom the descriptor), a real handle table with refcounts beside the existing\npersistent-root set, root ranges for data sections.\n\nGate: ash conformance unchanged across interpreter, AOT and wasm; benchmark\ndeltas within noise. The GC-stress and trigger env vars stay.","files":null}]}